    "answer": {
      "short": "Peaches: $\\$3$ per kg; pears: $\\$4$ per kg; plums: $\\$5$ per kg.",
      "worked": "Let $p$, $q$ and $r$ be the prices per kilogram of peaches, pears and plums, respectively, in dollars.\n$$\\begin{align*}p+2q+3r&=26\\qquad(1)\\\\p+q+2r&=17\\qquad(2)\\\\p+4q+r&=24\\qquad(3)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (2) from (1) and from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}q+r&=9\\qquad(4)\\\\3q-r&=7\\qquad(5)\\end{align*}$$\nAdd (4) and (5):\n$$\\begin{align*}4q&=16\\\\q&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $q=4$ into (4):\n$$\\begin{align*}4+r&=9\\\\r&=5\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $q=4$ and $r=5$ into (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}p+4+2(5)&=17\\\\p+14&=17\\\\p&=3\\end{align*}$$\nPeaches cost $\\$3$ per kg, pears cost $\\$4$ per kg and plums cost $\\$5$ per kg.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
